<title>HUNGARY: Budapest BSE to include Horizon on BUX.</title>
<headline>Budapest BSE to include Horizon on BUX.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Budapest Stock Exchange (BSE) said on Wednesday it would drop three stocks, Domus, Dunaholding and Styl, from the BUX index basket from April 1 but would add a new one.</p>
<p>The base price for the new stock, Horizon-Multiplan, will be fixed on March 28, the BSE said in a statement.</p>
<p>The BSE's council decided on the new composition of the BUX index basket at its meeting on March 3, it said.</p>
<p>The bourse gave no explanation for the changes. However, it reviews the index basket twice a year.</p>
<p>After the changes the BUX index basket comprises the following stocks: MOL, Richter, OTP Bank, Egis, BorsodChem, TVK, Danubius, Primagaz, Graboplast, Pannonplast, Pick, Zalakeramia, Inter-Europa Bank, Skala-Coop &quot;T&quot;, Zwack, Human, Fotex, Csopak, Horizon-Multiplan, Globus, Eravis and the Global Depositary Receipts of Cofinec.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
